    rdfs:label "Evidence for Pearl and Pot Ashes used in Soap Manufacture: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section THE OIL PALM"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Spanish or Castile soap is made by mixing olive oil and soda, while soft soap is made by mixing the oil with potash."@en ;
